            <div xml:id="d126">

                <pb facs="0295" n="207" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg207"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.G Women’s Rights/25: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Uruguay</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wright</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-12-27T16:00:00-05:00">December 27, 1933—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>32. Secretary’s telegram No. 82, December 23, 1 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Report by cable whether American Delegation signed Convention on
                        Nationality of Women.</item>
                    <pb facs="0296" n="208" xml:id="pg208"/>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Also cable what action was taken by the Conference and American Delegation
                        on the general convention on nationality (Topic 6 (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >f</hi>) of Agenda)<anchor n="48" xml:id="d126-f1"/></item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
